ive in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for the current Pallas maintenance contract (EC-0006-25, 220,914 ADA). The current contract is on track, with…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**USD peg is not aggressive**\nPeg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\n\nProposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) pegs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record cla…51:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"usd-peg-not-aggressive\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"USD peg is not aggressive\",\"body\":\"Proposals often denominate in USD at a chosen ADA price. If that peg is significantly below current market, the proposer is asking for more ADA than the same USD cost would actually require — an implicit overage. Conservative (at or above market) and neutral (within 5%) p"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"egs are fine; aggressive pegs (more than 5% below market) are flagged.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Peg is conservative or neutral vs market — not requesting more ADA than spot would imply.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$7b\"}]}],\"$L7c\"]}],\"$L7d\",\"$L7e\",\"$L7f\"]}]\n80:Tdc0,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Pallas by TxPipe: Maintaining Cardano's Core Rust Libraries, Year 2\nProposer: TxPipe\nAbstract: This proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Pallas\u0026#32;**([https://github.com/txpipe/pallas](https://github.com/txpipe/pallas)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD, continuing the open-source maintenance initiative funded through Intersect's treasury process in the previous cycle. The new grant period would begin after the closure of the existing contract, ensuring uninterrupted maintenance coverage.\n\nPallas is a collection of Rust crates that re-implement core Ouroboros and Cardano primitives: CBOR encoding,…\n\nFull proposal JSON (fetch this — the user-facing Hydra page is a JS-rendered SPA and bots see an empty shell):\nhttps://hydra-voting.intersectmbo.org/api/v0/proposals/69f8c6dec9c351b28aa8d7b8\n\n# Hydra proposal summary (from the proposer)\nThis proposal requests 420,000 ADA (plus a 105,000 ADA contingency reserve) to fund **a part-time maintainer for Pallas\u0026#32;**([https://github.com/txpipe/pallas](https://github.com/txpipe/pallas)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD, continuing the open-source maintenance initiative funded through Intersect's treasury process in the previous cycle. The new grant period would begin after the closure of the existing contract, ensuring uninterrupted maintenance coverage.\n\nPallas is a collection of Rust crates that re-implement core Ouroboros and Cardano primitives: CBOR encoding, cryptographic operations, mini-protocol networking, multi-era ledger traversal, transaction building, and address handling. These crates serve as shared infrastructure for projects like Aiken, Dolos, Lucid, Oura, Mithril, Amaru and many others across the ecosystem.\n\nWith over 649 pull requests, 199…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for the current Pallas maintenance contract (EC-0006-25, 220,914 ADA). The current contract is on track, with…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Treasury favourability is strong/moderate**\nAI-assigned favourability rubric — strong or moderate (not weak/none).\n\nThe return clause itself is rated strong or moderate (not weak or none). Strong means multiple substantive return mechanisms — price-peg surplus, unspent funds, revenue share — with concrete triggers and deadlines. Weak means vague promises with no enforcement.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"U