er for Pallas\u0026#32;**([https://github.com/txpipe/pallas](https://github.com/txpipe/pallas)) over 12 months at an annual rate of $105,000 USD, continuing the open-source maintenance initiative funded through Intersect's treasury process in the previous cycle. The new grant period would begin after the closure of the existing contract, ensuring uninterrupted maintenance coverage.\n\nPallas is a collection of Rust crates that re-implement core Ouroboros and Cardano primitives: CBOR encoding, cryptographic operations, mini-protocol networking, multi-era ledger traversal, transaction building, and address handling. These crates serve as shared infrastructure for projects like Aiken, Dolos, Lucid, Oura, Mithril, Amaru and many others across the ecosystem.\n\nWith over 649 pull requests, 199…\n\n# Track record claimed by the prop"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"oser\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for the current Pallas maintenance contract (EC-0006-25, 220,914 ADA). The current contract is on track, with…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Measurable on-chain KPIs**\nProposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\n\nJudgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the crite…59:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"measurable-onchain-kpis\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-3 pr-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-baseline font-medium\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\"}],[\"$\",\"$L22\",null,{\"label\":\"Measurable on-chain KPIs\",\"body\":\"Judgment call: does the proposal commit to specific on-chain KPIs that anyone can verify directly from the chain? Strong looks like 'X mainnet transactions per month, Y unique wallets, Z dApps integrated, all queryable via blockfrost or db-sync'. Weak looks like 'increase Cardano adoption', 'community growth', 'GitHub stars', or any metric the proposer themselves controls. On-chain metrics are tamper-proof and let the community measure delivery against the actual ledger, not the proposer's self-reported numbers.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-0.5 text-sm text-[color:var(--fg-muted)]\",\"children\":\"Proposal commits to specific, verifiable on-chain outcomes -- transactions, unique wallets, mainnet deployments, TVL -- not just GitHub commits or off-chain deliverables.\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$L35\",null,{\"prompt\":\"$8a\"}]}],\"$L8b\"]}],\"$L8c\",\"$L8d\",\"$L8e\"]}]\n8f:Tdae,I'm a Cardano DRep evaluating a 2026 treasury proposal. I need your help checking ONE specific criterion against this proposal. Please research the team and project before answering.\n# Proposal\nTitle: Pallas by TxPipe: Maintaining Cardano's Core Rust Libraries, Year 2\nProposer: TxPipe\nAbs