t crates that re-implement core Ouroboros and Cardano primitives: CBOR encoding, cryptographic operations, mini-protocol networking, multi-era ledger traversal, transaction building, and address handling. These crates serve as shared infrastructure for projects like Aiken, Dolos, Lucid, Oura, Mithril, Amaru and many others across the ecosystem.\n\nWith over 649 pull requests, 199…\n\n# Track record claimed by the proposer\nTxPipe is a Cardano-native infrastructure company focused on building open-source developer tooling in Rust. The team has been active in the Cardano ecosystem since 2021, maintaining a portfolio of interconnected tools that serve as foundational infrastructure for Rust-based development on Cardano.\n\nTxPipe has received funding through multiple Cardano ecosystem programs, including Project Catalyst (Funds 9 through 14) for various tooling initiatives, and Intersect's budget process for the current Pallas maintenance contract (EC-0006-25, 220,914 ADA). The current contract is on track, with…\n# Criterion to evaluate\n**Milestone schedule detailed (amounts + dates)**\nEach milestone has both an ADA amount and a target date.\n\nEach milestone has both a specific ADA amount and a target date. Less detailed schedules (amounts only, names only, none) give the proposer wiggle room. Dated amounts let everyone — proposer, DRep, community — track delivery against the plan.\n# What I need from you\n1. Verdict: YES / NO / UNCLEAR — does this proposal meet the criterion?\n2. Confidence: LOW / MEDIUM / HIGH\n3. A short rationale (3–6 sentences) citing sources you actually checked (GitHub repos, Catalyst project pages, X/Twitter accounts, articles). Be honest if the public info is thin or the proposer's track-record claims need independent verification.\nPlease err on the side of \"UNCLEAR\" with explanation rather than confident-but…5b:[\"$\",\"tr\",\"milestone-schedule-detailed\",{\"className\":\"border-b border-[color:var(--border)] align-top last:border-0\"